IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mig-visas`

-- Migration Act 1958 (with the Migration Regulations 1994), the visa applicant's and visa holder's questions -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case; the deposited Migration Regulations 1994 were read, no other instrument.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_migration-act-1958_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts are from the Western Australian life of Daniel (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel): Priya Nair,
-- Indian, on a student visa since 2019, marries Daniel (an Australian citizen) on 30 Nov 2024; d033 (10 Jan 2025) her
-- partner visa; d035 (9 Jan 2027) her permanent visa granted days before the London year; d047 (1 Feb 2032) Jarrah
-- sponsors a machine-learning engineer from Chennai on a Skills in Demand visa. Figures marked HYPOTHETICAL are
-- invented for the case; facts marked ASSUMED or INFERRED are not stated by the scenario.

`Priya and Daniel, married by a celebrant and living together` MEANS `Our relationship` WITH
    `we are married under a marriage valid for the Act` IS TRUE
    `we are committed to a shared life to the exclusion of all others` IS TRUE
    `our relationship is genuine and continuing` IS TRUE
    `we live together` IS TRUE
    `we live separately and apart on a permanent basis` IS FALSE
    `we are related by family` IS FALSE

`a couple joined only by a ceremony with no legal effect` MEANS `Our relationship` WITH
    `we are married under a marriage valid for the Act` IS FALSE
    `we are committed to a shared life to the exclusion of all others` IS TRUE
    `our relationship is genuine and continuing` IS TRUE
    `we live together` IS TRUE
    `we live separately and apart on a permanent basis` IS FALSE
    `we are related by family` IS FALSE

`Priya applying on her student visa (d033)` MEANS `Partner application` WITH
    `I hold a transit visa` IS FALSE
    `my partner is an Australian citizen, permanent resident or eligible New Zealand citizen` IS TRUE
    `my partner is barred from sponsoring by 820.211(2B)` IS FALSE
    `I am sponsored by my partner, or by their parent or guardian if they are under 18` IS TRUE
    `I hold a substantive visa` IS TRUE
    `I meet Schedule 3 criteria 3001, 3003 and 3004 or the Minister waives them` IS FALSE

`Priya two years after applying, together two years when she applied (ASSUMED)` MEANS `Permanent partner facts` WITH
    `I hold the temporary partner visa` IS TRUE
    `my partner still sponsors me` IS TRUE
    `I am still my partner's spouse or de facto partner` IS TRUE
    `years since I applied` IS 2
    `years our relationship had lasted when I applied` IS 2
    `we have a dependent child together` IS FALSE
    `my partner has died and we would have stayed together` IS FALSE
    `we separated after family violence by my partner, or with a child order` IS FALSE
    `I meet the public interest criteria` IS TRUE

`Priya granted days short of two years, together two years when she applied (ASSUMED)` MEANS `Permanent partner facts` WITH
    `I hold the temporary partner visa` IS TRUE
    `my partner still sponsors me` IS TRUE
    `I am still my partner's spouse or de facto partner` IS TRUE
    `years since I applied` IS 1.99
    `years our relationship had lasted when I applied` IS 2
    `we have a dependent child together` IS FALSE
    `my partner has died and we would have stayed together` IS FALSE
    `we separated after family violence by my partner, or with a child order` IS FALSE
    `I meet the public interest criteria` IS TRUE

`Priya granted days short of two years, together three years when she applied (ASSUMED)` MEANS `Permanent partner facts` WITH
    `I hold the temporary partner visa` IS TRUE
    `my partner still sponsors me` IS TRUE
    `I am still my partner's spouse or de facto partner` IS TRUE
    `years since I applied` IS 1.99
    `years our relationship had lasted when I applied` IS 3
    `we have a dependent child together` IS FALSE
    `my partner has died and we would have stayed together` IS FALSE
    `we separated after family violence by my partner, or with a child order` IS FALSE
    `I meet the public interest criteria` IS TRUE

`Priya days after her permanent visa, with ties (d035)` MEANS `Resident return facts` WITH
    `I hold a permanent visa, or lost my citizenship, or my last permanent visa ended without cancellation` IS TRUE
    `years in the last 5 I was here as a permanent visa holder or citizen` IS 0.02
    `the Minister is satisfied I have substantial ties of benefit to Australia` IS TRUE
    `I have been away for 5 continuous years without compelling reasons` IS FALSE

`a permanent resident of three years` MEANS `Resident return facts` WITH
    `I hold a permanent visa, or lost my citizenship, or my last permanent visa ended without cancellation` IS TRUE
    `years in the last 5 I was here as a permanent visa holder or citizen` IS 3
    `the Minister is satisfied I have substantial ties of benefit to Australia` IS FALSE
    `I have been away for 5 continuous years without compelling reasons` IS FALSE

`the engineer in Chennai, nominated by Jarrah (d047)` MEANS `Skills in Demand application` WITH
    `an occupation has been nominated for me in a stream` IS TRUE
    `I apply in the stream it was nominated for` IS TRUE
    `my application identifies the nomination` IS TRUE
    `the nomination is approved and its approval has not ceased, or is undecided` IS TRUE
    `my nominator is barred under s 140M` IS FALSE
    `I am in immigration clearance` IS FALSE
    `I am in Australia` IS FALSE
    `I hold a substantive visa or a Bridging A, B or C visa` IS FALSE

`the engineer from Chennai with four years' experience (d047, HYPOTHETICAL)` MEANS `Skills in Demand criteria` WITH
    `I am in Australia` IS FALSE
    `I substantially complied with my last visas' conditions` IS FALSE
    `the nomination is approved, by an approved sponsor, and has not ceased` IS TRUE
    `my intention and the position are genuine` IS TRUE
    `I paid or took a benefit for sponsorship in the last 3 years` IS FALSE
    `the Minister disregards that conduct` IS FALSE
    `I have adequate health insurance arrangements` IS TRUE
    `there is no adverse information about my nominator, or it is disregarded` IS TRUE
    `I meet the public interest and special return criteria` IS TRUE
    `months of full-time work in the occupation in the last 5 years` IS 48
    `the Minister considers I have the skills needed` IS TRUE
    `I meet the language requirements` IS TRUE
    `I am employed in the occupation in the sponsor's business or an associate's` IS TRUE

`an engineer who paid for his nomination` MEANS `Skills in Demand criteria` WITH
    `I am in Australia` IS FALSE
    `I substantially complied with my last visas' conditions` IS FALSE
    `the nomination is approved, by an approved sponsor, and has not ceased` IS TRUE
    `my intention and the position are genuine` IS TRUE
    `I paid or took a benefit for sponsorship in the last 3 years` IS TRUE
    `the Minister disregards that conduct` IS FALSE
    `I have adequate health insurance arrangements` IS TRUE
    `there is no adverse information about my nominator, or it is disregarded` IS TRUE
    `I meet the public interest and special return criteria` IS TRUE
    `months of full-time work in the occupation in the last 5 years` IS 48
    `the Minister considers I have the skills needed` IS TRUE
    `I meet the language requirements` IS TRUE
    `I am employed in the occupation in the sponsor's business or an associate's` IS TRUE

§ `ss 13, 14, 42 -- do I need a visa`

-- d047: the engineer in Chennai is not a citizen; on arrival without a visa in effect he would be unlawful.
#ASSERT `Must I hold a visa to travel to Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `Am I an unlawful non-citizen` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- d033: Priya on her Bridging A is lawful.
#ASSERT `Am I a lawful non-citizen` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 30, 5F, 5CB -- what visa, what relationship`

-- d033/d035: the 820 lasts until the 801 is decided (an event), the 801 indefinitely.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my visa permanent` `until a specified event happens`

#ASSERT `Am I my partner's spouse` `Priya and Daniel, married by a celebrant and living together`

#ASSERT `Am I my partner's de facto partner` `a couple joined only by a ceremony with no legal effect`

§ `Sch 1 item 1214C; Sch 2 Part 820; s 65 -- the temporary partner visa (d033)`

#ASSERT `May I apply for the temporary partner visa in Australia` TRUE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `Do I meet the temporary partner visa criteria when I apply` `Priya and Daniel, married by a celebrant and living together` `Priya applying on her student visa (d033)`

#ASSERT `Must my temporary partner visa be granted` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the visa must be granted`
#ASSERT `Must my temporary partner visa be granted` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the visa must be refused`

-- d033: once the 820 is granted Priya may work without limit.
#ASSERT NOT `Does my partner visa carry any condition` 

§ `Sch 2 Part 010; Sch 8 condition 8105 -- the Bridging A while she waits (d033)`

#ASSERT `Do I meet the Bridging A criteria` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `How many days after the decision may I stay on my Bridging A visa` `it was granted` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How many days after the decision may I stay on my Bridging A visa` `it was refused` EQUALS 35

-- d033: her student visa carried 8105 (cl 500.611); her Bridging A carries it, at 40 hours, not the student's 48.
#ASSERT `Does my Bridging A carry my last visa's work limit` TRUE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `How many hours a fortnight may I work in session` `a bridging visa granted on another application` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `How many hours a fortnight may I work in session` `a Student visa (subclass 500)` EQUALS 48

§ `s 82 -- which visa ends`

-- d033: the student visa ends when the 820 comes into effect, and so does the Bridging A; the Bridging A coming into effect ends nothing.
#ASSERT `Does my visa end when the new one comes into effect` `an ordinary substantive visa` `an ordinary substantive visa`
#ASSERT NOT `Does my visa end when the new one comes into effect` `an ordinary substantive visa` `a bridging visa`

-- Leaving on the Bridging A (remain only, granted in Australia) ends it; leaving on the 801 within its travel period does not.
#ASSERT `Does my visa end when I leave` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my visa end when I leave` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- d035: Priya re-enters from London inside the 801's five years and is in Australia when they end: the visa holds.
#ASSERT NOT `Does my visa end when its travel period ends` TRUE TRUE

§ `Sch 2 Part 801; reg 1.03 -- the permanent partner visa (d033, d035)`

#ASSERT `Was I in a long-term partner relationship` 3 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Was I in a long-term partner relationship` 2 FALSE

-- d035: granted "days before" 9 Jan 2027 on an application INFERRED as 10 Jan 2025 -- under two years -- the grant needs a
-- long-term partner relationship when she applied (cl 801.221(6A)).
#ASSERT `Do I meet the permanent partner visa criteria` `Priya two years after applying, together two years when she applied (ASSUMED)`
#ASSERT NOT `Do I meet the permanent partner visa criteria` `Priya granted days short of two years, together two years when she applied (ASSUMED)`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the permanent partner visa criteria` `Priya granted days short of two years, together three years when she applied (ASSUMED)`

#ASSERT `Am I an Australian permanent resident` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 79, 81(2), 82(6); cl 801.511; Part 155 -- leaving and coming back (d035)`

#ASSERT `For how many years may I travel on my permanent partner visa`  EQUALS 5

-- d035: leaving a week after the grant, back about 14 months later (INFERRED from the London year): the 801 carries her back.
#ASSERT `May I come back on my visa` TRUE 5 0.02 1.2

#ASSERT NOT `Do I need a resident return visa` TRUE 5 0.02 1.2
#ASSERT `Do I need a resident return visa` TRUE 5 4.5 5.5

-- d035: the resident return visa she took could give her one year at most -- less than the 801's five.
#ASSERT `How many years would a resident return visa give me` `Priya days after her permanent visa, with ties (d035)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How many years would a resident return visa give me` `a permanent resident of three years` EQUALS 5

#ASSERT `What is the resident return visa charge` FALSE EQUALS 1475

